Evaluation Methology
Companies are evaluated based on quantitative and qualitative indicators for each RegenMark.
Scores for each indicator are normalized on a scale of 0-100 based on industry standards and best practices.
The final RegenMark score is an average of all indicator scores, determining the level of sustainability achieved.

To fine-tune the scoring model, we should integrate industry benchmarks, regulatory frameworks, and best practices for each RegenMark. Below is a refined point system that aligns with globally recognized sustainability standards such as:
GHG Protocol, SBTi (Science-Based Targets Initiative) – for Carbon Saver
ISO 14046, Water Footprint Network – for Water Guardian
Ellen MacArthur Foundation Circularity Metrics – for Circular Champion
ILO (International Labour Organization) & UN Global Compact – for Human First
Leaping Bunny, PETA, and Fair Trade Certifications – for Humane Hero




